IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 112 to 117 -- THE NUMBER OF
-- DIRECTORS, NOTICE OF CHANGE, MEETINGS OF DIRECTORS, DELEGATION, VALIDITY OF ACTS AND RESOLUTIONS IN LIEU OF A
-- MEETING. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A fact that another module
-- of this piece works out is a plain input and the comment names the rule. A cross-reference to another piece is
-- a plain input and says so. "Prescribed" and "the regulations" are plain inputs.

§ `s 112 Number of directors`

§§ `s 112(1) Number of directors`

-- out of range: section 173 (piece cb4) is the procedure for amending the articles; this rule is the limit on
-- what the amendment may do. "Subject to paragraph 107(h)": where the articles provide for cumulative voting a
-- decrease also needs the vote that paragraph sets (`the vote needed to decrease the number of directors is met
-- within s 107(h)`, in cb2-part10-election).
-- src:1340 | Number of directors
-- src:1341 | 112 (1) The shareholders of a corporation may amend the articles to increase or, subject to paragraph 107(h), to decrease the number of directors, or the minimum or maximum number of directors, but no decrease shall shorten the term of an incumbent director.
@ref CBCA s 112(1) (src:1340-1341)
GIVEN `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may amend the articles to change the number of directors within s 112(1)` MEANS
    NOT `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors`
    OR (        (   NOT `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
                 OR `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)`)
            AND (NOT `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director`))

§§ `s 112(2) Election of directors where articles amended`

-- src:1342 | Election of directors where articles amended
-- src:1343 | (2) Where the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles of a corporation to increase or, subject to paragraph 107(h) and to subsection (1), decrease the number or minimum or maximum number of directors, the shareholders may, at the meeting, elect the number of directors authorized by the amendment, and for that purpose, notwithstanding subsections 179(1) and 262(3), on the issue of a certificate of amendment the articles are deemed to be amended as of the date the shareholders adopt the amendment.
@ref CBCA s 112(2) (src:1342-1343)
GIVEN `the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may elect the number of directors authorized by the amendment at the meeting within s 112(2)` MEANS
        `the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles`
    AND `the shareholders may amend the articles to change the number of directors within s 112(1)`
            `the amendment decreases the number or the minimum or maximum number of directors`
            `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
            `the votes cast meet the threshold in paragraph 107(h)`
            `the decrease would shorten the term of an incumbent director`

-- NOTHING: no certificate of amendment has issued, so the articles are not yet deemed amended. out of range:
-- section 179(1) (piece cb4); out of range: section 262(3) (piece cb5), which this subsection displaces for the purpose.
-- src:1342 | Election of directors where articles amended
-- src:1343 | (2) Where the shareholders at a meeting adopt an amendment to the articles of a corporation to increase or, subject to paragraph 107(h) and to subsection (1), decrease the number or minimum or maximum number of directors, the shareholders may, at the meeting, elect the number of directors authorized by the amendment, and for that purpose, notwithstanding subsections 179(1) and 262(3), on the issue of a certificate of amendment the articles are deemed to be amended as of the date the shareholders adopt the amendment.
@ref CBCA s 112(2) (src:1342-1343)
GIVEN `a certificate of amendment has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the shareholders adopt the amendment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date as of which the articles are deemed amended within s 112(2)` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of amendment has been issued`
    THEN JUST `the date the shareholders adopt the amendment`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 113 Notice of change of director or director's address`

§§ `s 113(1) Notice of change of director or director's address`

-- Fifteen days counted by the keel's convention (fork F1): the last day is the event date plus fifteen.
-- src:1344 | Notice of change of director or director’s address
-- src:1345 | 113 (1) A corporation shall, within fifteen days after
-- src:1346 | (a) a change is made among its directors, or
-- src:1347 | (b) it receives a notice of change of address of a director referred to in subsection (1.1),
-- src:1348 | send to the Director a notice, in the form that the Director fixes, setting out the change, and the Director shall file the notice.
@ref CBCA s 113(1) (src:1344-1348)
GIVEN `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to send the notice to the Director within s 113(1)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`)
        `counted from` `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director`

-- src:1344 | Notice of change of director or director’s address
-- src:1345 | 113 (1) A corporation shall, within fifteen days after
-- src:1346 | (a) a change is made among its directors, or
-- src:1347 | (b) it receives a notice of change of address of a director referred to in subsection (1.1),
-- src:1348 | send to the Director a notice, in the form that the Director fixes, setting out the change, and the Director shall file the notice.
@ref CBCA s 113(1) (src:1344-1348)
GIVEN `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation sent the notice to the Director` IS A DATE
      `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice sets out the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has sent the notice to the Director as required within s 113(1)` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`)
            `the date of the change among the directors, or of the receipt of the notice of change of address of a director`
            `the date the corporation sent the notice to the Director`
    AND `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes`
    AND `the notice sets out the change`

-- src:1344 | Notice of change of director or director’s address
-- src:1345 | 113 (1) A corporation shall, within fifteen days after
-- src:1346 | (a) a change is made among its directors, or
-- src:1347 | (b) it receives a notice of change of address of a director referred to in subsection (1.1),
-- src:1348 | send to the Director a notice, in the form that the Director fixes, setting out the change, and the Director shall file the notice.
@ref CBCA s 113(1) (src:1344-1348)
GIVEN `the Director has received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must file the notice of change within s 113(1)` MEANS
    `the Director has received the notice`

§§ `s 113(1.1) Director's change of address`

-- src:1349 | Director’s change of address
-- src:1350 | (1.1) A director shall, within fifteen days after changing his or her address, send the corporation a notice of that change.
@ref CBCA s 113(1.1) (src:1349-1350)
GIVEN `the date the director changed their address` IS A DATE
      `the date the director sent the corporation notice of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director has sent the corporation notice of the change of address as required within s 113(1.1)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`)
        `the date the director changed their address`
        `the date the director sent the corporation notice of the change`

§§ `s 113(2) Application to court`

-- src:1351 | Application to court
-- src:1352 | (2) Any interested person, or the Director, may apply to a court for an order to require a corporation to comply with subsection (1), and the court may so order and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 113(2) (src:1351-1352)
GIVEN `the person is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may apply to a court for an order requiring the corporation to comply with subsection 113(1) within s 113(2)` MEANS
        `the person is an interested person`
    OR  `the person is the Director`

-- The court "may so order": the order presupposes an application and that the corporation has not complied.
-- src:1351 | Application to court
-- src:1352 | (2) Any interested person, or the Director, may apply to a court for an order to require a corporation to comply with subsection (1), and the court may so order and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 113(2) (src:1351-1352)
GIVEN `a person entitled to do so under subsection 113(2) has applied to a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has not complied with subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order the corporation to comply and make any further order it thinks fit within s 113(2)` MEANS
        `a person entitled to do so under subsection 113(2) has applied to a court`
    AND `the corporation has not complied with subsection 113(1)`

§ `s 114 Meeting of directors`

§§ `s 114(1) Meeting of directors`

-- src:1353 | Meeting of directors
-- src:1354 | 114 (1) Unless the articles or by-laws otherwise provide, the directors may meet at any place and on such notice as the by-laws require.
@ref CBCA s 114(1) (src:1353-1354)
GIVEN `the articles or by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may meet at any place and on such notice as the by-laws require within s 114(1)` MEANS
    NOT `the articles or by-laws otherwise provide`

§§ `s 114(2) Quorum`

-- "A majority of the number of directors or minimum number of directors required by the articles": more than
-- half of that number. "Subject to the articles or by-laws": they may fix a different number.
-- src:1355 | Quorum
-- src:1356 | (2) Subject to the articles or by-laws, a majority of the number of directors or minimum number of directors required by the articles constitutes a quorum at any meeting of directors, and, notwithstanding any vacancy among the directors, a quorum of directors may exercise all the powers of the directors.
@ref CBCA s 114(2) (src:1355-1356)
GIVEN `the number of directors, or the minimum number of directors, required by the articles` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`there is a quorum of directors within s 114(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of directors the articles or by-laws fix as the quorum, if they fix one`
    WHEN JUST q THEN `the number of directors present` AT LEAST q
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the number of directors present` GREATER THAN (`the number of directors, or the minimum number of directors, required by the articles` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- src:1355 | Quorum
-- src:1356 | (2) Subject to the articles or by-laws, a majority of the number of directors or minimum number of directors required by the articles constitutes a quorum at any meeting of directors, and, notwithstanding any vacancy among the directors, a quorum of directors may exercise all the powers of the directors.
@ref CBCA s 114(2) (src:1355-1356)
GIVEN `there is a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a quorum of directors may exercise all the powers of the directors despite any vacancy within s 114(2)` MEANS
    `there is a quorum of directors`

§§ `s 114(3) Canadian directors present at meetings`

-- Directors "other than directors of a corporation referred to in subsection 105(4)" (the holding-corporation
-- exception, `the exception applies within s 105(4)` in cb2-part10-qualification) are not so restricted.
-- (a) the corporation is subject to s 105(3): at least 25 per cent of the directors present are resident
-- Canadians, or one if the corporation has less than four directors. (b) subject to s 105(3.1): a majority of
-- the directors present, or one if the corporation has only two directors.
-- src:1357 | Canadian directors present at meetings
-- src:1358 | (3) Directors, other than directors of a corporation referred to in subsection 105(4), shall not transact business at a meeting of directors unless,
-- src:1359 | (a) if the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3), at least twenty-five per cent of the directors present are resident Canadians or, if the corporation has less than four directors, at least one of the directors present is a resident Canadian; or
-- src:1360 | (b) if the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1), a majority of directors present are resident Canadians or if the corporation has only two directors, at least one of the directors present is a resident Canadian.
@ref CBCA s 114(3) (src:1357-1360)
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may transact business under subsection 114(3) within s 114(3)` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)`
         THEN (IF `the number of directors of the corporation` EQUALS 2
               THEN `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` AT LEAST 1
               ELSE (`the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `the number of directors present`)
         ELSE (IF `the number of directors of the corporation` LESS THAN 4
               THEN `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` AT LEAST 1
               ELSE `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` AT LEAST (25% TIMES `the number of directors present`))

§§ `s 114(4) Exception`

-- (b) is worked out by asking subsection (3) again with the absent resident Canadian director counted present.
-- src:1361 | Exception
-- src:1362 | (4) Despite subsection (3), directors may transact business at a meeting of directors where the number of resident Canadian directors, required under that subsection, is not present if
-- src:1363 | (a) a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting; and
-- src:1364 | (b) the required number of resident Canadian directors would have been present had that director been present at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(4) (src:1361-1364)
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER
      `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may transact business despite subsection 114(3) within s 114(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the directors may transact business under subsection 114(3) within s 114(3)`
                 `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies`
                 `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)`
                 `the number of directors of the corporation`
                 `the number of directors present`
                 `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians`)
    AND `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting`
    AND `the directors may transact business under subsection 114(3) within s 114(3)`
            `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies`
            `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)`
            `the number of directors of the corporation`
            (`the number of directors present` PLUS 1)
            (`the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` PLUS 1)

-- src:1357 | Canadian directors present at meetings
-- src:1358 | (3) Directors, other than directors of a corporation referred to in subsection 105(4), shall not transact business at a meeting of directors unless,
-- src:1359 | (a) if the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3), at least twenty-five per cent of the directors present are resident Canadians or, if the corporation has less than four directors, at least one of the directors present is a resident Canadian; or
-- src:1360 | (b) if the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1), a majority of directors present are resident Canadians or if the corporation has only two directors, at least one of the directors present is a resident Canadian.
-- src:1361 | Exception
-- src:1362 | (4) Despite subsection (3), directors may transact business at a meeting of directors where the number of resident Canadian directors, required under that subsection, is not present if
-- src:1363 | (a) a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting; and
-- src:1364 | (b) the required number of resident Canadian directors would have been present had that director been present at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(3) s 114(4) (src:1357-1364)
GIVEN `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians` IS A NUMBER
      `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may transact business at the meeting within s 114(3) and (4)` MEANS
        `the directors may transact business under subsection 114(3) within s 114(3)`
            `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies`
            `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)`
            `the number of directors of the corporation`
            `the number of directors present`
            `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians`
    OR  `the directors may transact business despite subsection 114(3) within s 114(4)`
            `the corporation is one to which subsection 105(4) applies`
            `the corporation is subject to subsection 105(3.1)`
            `the number of directors of the corporation`
            `the number of directors present`
            `the number of directors present who are resident Canadians`
            `a resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves in writing, or by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, the business transacted at the meeting`

§§ `s 114(5) Notice of meeting`

-- Section 115(3) is in this module (`the managing director or committee has authority to exercise the power
-- within s 115(3)`); the matters it lists must be specified in the notice, and the by-laws may require more.
-- src:1365 | Notice of meeting
-- src:1366 | (5) A notice of a meeting of directors shall specify any matter referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting but, unless the by-laws otherwise provide, need not specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(5) (src:1365-1366)
GIVEN `the matter is one referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws require the notice to specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting must specify the matter within s 114(5)` MEANS
        `the matter is one referred to in subsection 115(3) that is to be dealt with at the meeting`
    OR  `the by-laws require the notice to specify the purpose of or the business to be transacted`

§§ `s 114(6) Waiver of notice`

-- src:1367 | Waiver of notice
-- src:1368 | (6) A director may in any manner waive a notice of a meeting of directors; and attendance of a director at a meeting of directors is a waiver of notice of the meeting, except where a director attends a meeting for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called.
@ref CBCA s 114(6) (src:1367-1368)
GIVEN `the director waived the notice in some manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director attended the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director has waived notice of the meeting within s 114(6)` MEANS
        `the director waived the notice in some manner`
    OR  (    `the director attended the meeting`
         AND (NOT `the director attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called`))

§§ `s 114(7) Adjournment`

-- src:1369 | Adjournment
-- src:1370 | (7) Notice of an adjourned meeting of directors is not required to be given if the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(7) (src:1369-1370)
GIVEN `the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the adjourned meeting of directors is not required within s 114(7)` MEANS
    `the time and place of the adjourned meeting is announced at the original meeting`

§§ `s 114(8) One director meeting`

-- src:1371 | One director meeting
-- src:1372 | (8) Where a corporation has only one director, that director may constitute a meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(8) (src:1371-1372)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the one director may constitute a meeting within s 114(8)` MEANS
    `the number of directors of the corporation` EQUALS 1

§§ `s 114(9) Participation`

-- src:1373 | Participation
-- src:1374 | (9) Subject to the by-laws, a director may, in accordance with the regulations, if any, and if all the directors of the corporation consent, participate in a meeting of directors or of a committee of directors by means of a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting. A director participating in such a meeting by such means is deemed for the purposes of this Act to be present at that meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(9) (src:1373-1374)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the corporation consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director may participate by a communication facility within s 114(9)` MEANS
        (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any`
    AND `all the directors of the corporation consent`
    AND `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting`

-- src:1373 | Participation
-- src:1374 | (9) Subject to the by-laws, a director may, in accordance with the regulations, if any, and if all the directors of the corporation consent, participate in a meeting of directors or of a committee of directors by means of a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting. A director participating in such a meeting by such means is deemed for the purposes of this Act to be present at that meeting.
@ref CBCA s 114(9) (src:1373-1374)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the corporation consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director participates in the meeting by that means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is deemed present at the meeting within s 114(9)` MEANS
        `the director participates in the meeting by that means`
    AND `the director may participate by a communication facility within s 114(9)`
            `the by-laws otherwise provide`
            `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any`
            `all the directors of the corporation consent`
            `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting`

§ `s 115 Delegation`

§§ `s 115(1) Delegation`

DECLARE `Delegate of the powers of the directors` IS ONE OF
    `a managing director appointed under s 115(1)`
    `a committee of directors appointed under s 115(1)`

-- src:1375 | Delegation
-- src:1376 | 115 (1) Directors of a corporation may appoint from their number a managing director who is a resident Canadian or a committee of directors and delegate to such managing director or committee any of the powers of the directors.
@ref CBCA s 115(1) (src:1375-1376)
GIVEN `the delegate` IS A `Delegate of the powers of the directors`
      `the delegate is appointed from the number of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the managing director is a resident Canadian` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may appoint the delegate and delegate powers to it within s 115(1)` MEANS
        `the delegate is appointed from the number of the directors`
    AND (CONSIDER `the delegate`
         WHEN `a managing director appointed under s 115(1)` THEN `the managing director is a resident Canadian`
         WHEN `a committee of directors appointed under s 115(1)` THEN TRUE)

§§ `s 115(3) Limits on authority`

-- out of range: section 27 (piece cb1); section 41 (piece cb1); section 155 (piece cb3); Part XIII (piece cb3); Part XVII (piece cb4).
-- Each is named only inside a power the directors keep; the constructors name them and nothing else is taken from them.
DECLARE `Power of the directors` IS ONE OF
    `submitting to the shareholders any question or matter requiring their approval`
    `filling a vacancy among the directors or in the office of auditor, or appointing additional directors`
    `issuing securities`
    `issuing shares of a series under section 27`
    `declaring dividends`
    `purchasing, redeeming or otherwise acquiring shares issued by the corporation`
    `paying a commission referred to in section 41`
    `approving a management proxy circular referred to in Part XIII`
    `approving a take-over bid circular or directors' circular referred to in Part XVII`
    `approving financial statements referred to in section 155`
    `adopting, amending or repealing by-laws`
    `any other power of the directors`

-- (c), (c.1) and (f) carry "except as authorized by the directors": the managing director or committee has
-- authority when the directors have authorized the act; (a), (b), (d), (e), (g) to (j) are never delegated.
-- src:1378 | Limits on authority
-- src:1379 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1), no managing director and no committee of directors has authority to
-- src:1380 | (a) submit to the shareholders any question or matter requiring the approval of the shareholders;
-- src:1381 | (b) fill a vacancy among the directors or in the office of auditor, or appoint additional directors;
-- src:1382 | (c) issue securities except as authorized by the directors;
-- src:1383 | (c.1) issue shares of a series under section 27 except as authorized by the directors;
-- src:1384 | (d) declare dividends;
-- src:1385 | (e) purchase, redeem or otherwise acquire shares issued by the corporation;
-- src:1386 | (f) pay a commission referred to in section 41 except as authorized by the directors;
-- src:1387 | (g) approve a management proxy circular referred to in Part XIII;
-- src:1388 | (h) approve a take-over bid circular or directors’ circular referred to in Part XVII;
-- src:1389 | (i) approve any financial statements referred to in section 155; or
-- src:1390 | (j) adopt, amend or repeal by-laws.
@ref CBCA s 115(3) (src:1378-1390)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `Power of the directors`
      `the directors have authorized the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the managing director or committee has authority to exercise the power within s 115(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `submitting to the shareholders any question or matter requiring their approval` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `filling a vacancy among the directors or in the office of auditor, or appointing additional directors` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `issuing securities` THEN `the directors have authorized the act`
    WHEN `issuing shares of a series under section 27` THEN `the directors have authorized the act`
    WHEN `declaring dividends` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `purchasing, redeeming or otherwise acquiring shares issued by the corporation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `paying a commission referred to in section 41` THEN `the directors have authorized the act`
    WHEN `approving a management proxy circular referred to in Part XIII` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `approving a take-over bid circular or directors' circular referred to in Part XVII` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `approving financial statements referred to in section 155` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `adopting, amending or repealing by-laws` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other power of the directors` THEN TRUE

§ `s 116 Validity of acts of directors and officers`

-- src:1391 | Validity of acts of directors and officers
-- src:1392 | 116 An act of a director or officer is valid notwithstanding an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification.
@ref CBCA s 116 (src:1391-1392)
GIVEN `the act is an act of a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground alleged is an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the irregularity or defect does not invalidate the act within s 116` MEANS
        `the act is an act of a director or officer`
    AND `the ground alleged is an irregularity in their election or appointment or a defect in their qualification`

§ `s 117 Resolution in lieu of meeting`

§§ `s 117(1) Resolution in lieu of meeting`

-- src:1393 | Resolution in lieu of meeting
-- src:1394 | 117 (1) A resolution in writing, signed by all the directors entitled to vote on that resolution at a meeting of directors or committee of directors, is as valid as if it had been passed at a meeting of directors or committee of directors.
@ref CBCA s 117(1) (src:1393-1394)
GIVEN `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the written resolution is as valid as if passed at a meeting within s 117(1)` MEANS
        `the resolution is in writing`
    AND `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it` EQUALS 0

§§ `s 117(2) Filing resolution`

-- src:1395 | Filing resolution
-- src:1396 | (2) A copy of every resolution referred to in subsection (1) shall be kept with the minutes of the proceedings of the directors or committee of directors.
@ref CBCA s 117(2) (src:1395-1396)
GIVEN `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a copy of the resolution must be kept with the minutes within s 117(2)` MEANS
    `the written resolution is as valid as if passed at a meeting within s 117(1)`
        `the resolution is in writing`
        `the number of directors entitled to vote on the resolution who did not sign it`

§§ `s 117(3) Evidence`

-- src:1397 | Evidence
-- src:1398 | (3) Unless a ballot is demanded, an entry in the minutes of a meeting to the effect that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the fact without proof of the number or proportion of the votes recorded in favour of or against the resolution.
@ref CBCA s 117(3) (src:1397-1398)
GIVEN `the minutes record that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ballot is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the minute entry is proof of the declared result without proof of the votes within s 117(3)` MEANS
        `the minutes record that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated`
    AND (NOT `a ballot is demanded`)
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
